Rule 11 (broadcasting compatibility of the first dimension for 2-dimensional inputs)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1
>>
Rule 12 (broadcasting compatibility of the second dimension for 2-dimensional inputs)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 then shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 1) ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 1) = 1
>>
Rule 15 (if neither input is a scalar, they must be broadcast compatible)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)))
>>
Rule 17 (if non-scalar inputs have the same rank, they must be broadcast-compatible along all dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 18 (if both inputs are 1-D, their single dimension must be broadcast-compatible)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1) then (shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1)
>>
Rule 19 (if both tensors are 2-D, their first dimensions must be broadcast-compatible)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2) then (shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1)
>>
Rule 20 (if both tensors are 2-D, their second dimensions must be broadcast-compatible)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2) then (shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 1) ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 1) = 1)
