Rule 21 (if the first tensor is at least 1-D and the second is 1-D, their trailing dimensions must be broadcast-compatible)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1) then (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1)
>>
Rule 22 (broadcast compatibility of trailing dimensions when the first tensor has a higher rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) + i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) + i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 23 (broadcast compatibility of trailing dimensions when the second tensor has a higher rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) > ndim(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) + i) = shape(v_1, i) ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) + i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1)
>>
